{"authored" [{"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/0b9c4ebc430e05ef205e3d8108f2e1649bbc51b1a6b54e8f47b48e7ddad1e9a6.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $L$ defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4{cos}^{3}⁡t,\\,y=4{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{cos}^{3}⁡t) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{sin}^{3}⁡t) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =12{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t)}^{2}+{(12{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t+144{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{144{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}12|\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/59704c6b8e643337113ab99b22eaeaac8d59ac3c15042409e8a0a8eac6ee54fd.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\frac{t}{2},\\,y={e}^{t}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{({e}^{2t})+(\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/4aa2bca8faab077c47fb968882579233babe7d323ba3120088e8ea5599fbd570.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={e}^{t},\\,y=t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "a65ee75ec87be7a519e93d5cfe49536c7a3d0c6a84a2a1a17a988596a7ad37df" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0" "basis" 1211 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/ref