353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cfb54ba431bdbe5d2817c0777f24df26b9a0580b1a48e193ae845a0f0f1beb5"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/assets/33939aec3ac1315771d36714d15b590980197aabf3c169cdea1a1108baf6d0fa.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{9}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cfb54ba431bdbe5d2817c0777f24df26b9a0580b1a48e193ae845a0f0f1beb5"} {"question" "q-351427" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351427" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/assets/da2526ff7031c9dbc704b59e60c65df14dcd0678427e02c386fc16a86e1fc89c.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{5},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1) \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25{cos}^{2}⁡t+25{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5t\\,{|}_{\\pi /5}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cfb54ba431bdbe5d2817c0777f24df26b9a0580b1a48e193ae845a0f0f1beb5"} {"question" "q-351428" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351428" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae15b2efdde2217aa39750eaee9b3f07fa5b293e652a5f6785073390c75e0159"} {"question" "q-351439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062586/assets/0b9c4ebc430e05ef205e3d8108f2e1649bbc51b1a6b54e8f47b